# @j0nathan-ll0yd/* (copy, fixtures, portal-contract, schemas, tokens, web, config)
# resolve from GitHub Packages. Registry mapping ONLY -- the auth token is
# intentionally NOT committed here (atlas decision 0032, baseline item 4).
# pnpm IGNORES an env-expanded `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}`
# in a project-level .npmrc and warns on every command; npm expanded it, pnpm
# does not. Local auth comes from the machine-global ~/.npmrc; CI sets it at the
# user level via `pnpm config set '//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken'` (see the
# "Authenticate to GitHub Packages" step in every installing workflow, and the
# equivalent step in scripts/run-in-docker.sh). See atlas decisions 0015, 0032.
#
# The former `legacy-peer-deps=true` line is npm-only; its intent now lives in
# pnpm-workspace.yaml as `strict-peer-dependencies: false` (same standing
# @vite-pwa/astro astro-7 peer workaround -- rationale is recorded there, next
# to the vite-plugin-pwa override it travels with).
@j0nathan-ll0yd:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
